# A raised-cosine offset: the shorter the bend, the larger the radiation loss.
# Reference: the same propagation stepped independently in NumPy. The pipeline checks that transmission rises with length.
title S-bend shifting a 0.5 um guide by 2 um over 40 um
window width=24 length=60
guide straight x=0 width=0.5 from=0 to=10
guide sbend x0=0 x1=2 width=0.5 from=10 to=50
guide straight x=2 width=0.5 from=50 to=60
launch mode x=0 width=0.5
monitor out z=60 x=2 width=0.5
plane end z=60
expect power out 0.999869352 2e-7
expect total end 0.999995543 2e-7
expect centroid end 2.0008950 2e-6
expect radius end 0.2819521 2e-6
expect neff 2.232755841 2e-8
